// A set or a map written over a type parameter asks that parameter for an
// ordering, because a set keeps its elements in order and a map keeps its keys
// in order. Saying `T is ord` is what promises one; every type there is
// satisfies it, so nothing is shut out, but the signature has to say so.
//
// The map's values are free: nothing puts them in order.
fun by_key<K, V>(ref m: %{K = V}): bool
    ret true
end fun
